sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as End user
    participant UserTool as user-cert-fetcher<br/>(user's local tool)
    participant IdP as Identity Provider<br/>(Keycloak / Okta / etc.)
    participant CredAgentObs as Credentials Agent<br/>(observer - low trust)
    participant Cassini as Cassini broker
    participant CredAgentCon as Credentials Agent<br/>(consumer - high trust)
    participant Ledger as LedgerActor<br/>(event log + derived state -<br/>the actual record of truth)
    participant CertIssuer as cert-issuer<br/>(never directly reachable<br/>by user-facing requests)
    participant CA as CA (in-process,<br/>part of cert-issuer)
    participant Projection as ProjectionActor<br/>(best-effort, fire-and-forget -<br/>never gates this agent's own health)
    participant Graph as Neo4j<br/>(rebuildable projection -<br/>observability only)

    participant App as A Polar app<br/>(e.g. ACE)

    Note over User,Graph: Fully automated. No admin presence required at<br/>request time - only a prior grant, made<br/>independently, at any earlier point.

    User->>UserTool: Run tool
    activate UserTool
    UserTool->>IdP: Authorization Code flow (unchanged)
    activate IdP
    IdP-->>User: Present login (password, smart card/PIV, MFA)
    User->>IdP: Authenticate directly with IdP
    IdP-->>UserTool: Access token (identity claims,<br/>used unmodified)
    deactivate IdP

    Note over UserTool,CertIssuer: Query the normalized identity first -<br/>see identity_normalization_query.mmd.<br/>The CSR's SAN must already match what<br/>cert-issuer's /issue will check before<br/>the CSR is ever submitted for signing.

    UserTool->>UserTool: Generate keypair locally<br/>(private key never leaves this machine),<br/>build CSR using the normalized identity<br/>as the DNS SAN

    UserTool->>CredAgentObs: POST /issue with the CSR<br/>and credential
    deactivate UserTool
    activate CredAgentObs
    CredAgentObs->>CredAgentObs: Well-formedness check on the CSR only -<br/>no token validation, no trust decision.<br/>The observer never touches signing<br/>key material or makes any judgment.
    CredAgentObs--)Cassini: Publish IssuanceRequest,<br/>tagged with a fresh correlation_id
    deactivate CredAgentObs
    activate Cassini

    Cassini--)CredAgentCon: Deliver
    deactivate Cassini
    activate CredAgentCon

    CredAgentCon->>IdP: Token introspection (RFC 7662) -<br/>local signature validation alone cannot<br/>detect a session revoked or logged out<br/>server-side before natural expiry
    activate IdP
    IdP-->>CredAgentCon: Still valid (or not)
    deactivate IdP

    CredAgentCon->>CertIssuer: POST /validate<br/>(direct, internal, core-to-core -<br/>both are trusted services)
    activate CertIssuer
    CertIssuer->>CertIssuer: Validate token for real (existing,<br/>already-tested multi-issuer oidc.rs<br/>logic - issuer selection, signature,<br/>audience, expiry, claim extraction)
    CertIssuer-->>CredAgentCon: Validated identity and instance_binding
    deactivate CertIssuer

    CredAgentCon->>Ledger: Check grant for this identity, and<br/>whether this exact identity and<br/>instance_binding pair already holds<br/>a currently valid, unrevoked<br/>certificate - an in-memory,<br/>race-free lookup against this<br/>actor's own derived state, never<br/>a graph read
    activate Ledger
    Ledger-->>CredAgentCon: Permissions (if granted) and<br/>renewal check result
    deactivate Ledger

    alt No existing valid cert for this identity and instance_binding
        CredAgentCon->>CertIssuer: POST /issue, with these<br/>permissions embedded in the<br/>SAN set
        activate CertIssuer
        CertIssuer->>CertIssuer: Combine identity (from token,<br/>unmodified) and permissions<br/>(from the grant, admin's final say)
        CertIssuer->>CA: Sign CSR
        activate CA
        CA-->>CertIssuer: Signed certificate
        deactivate CA
        CertIssuer-->>CredAgentCon: Signed certificate
        deactivate CertIssuer
        CredAgentCon->>Ledger: Append issuance-completed event
        activate Ledger
        Ledger->>Ledger: fsync'd to the event log first<br/>(hash includes previous entry's<br/>hash - the actual record - if<br/>this grant was used, it's<br/>consumed as of this event),<br/>then folded into derived state
        Ledger--)Projection: Notify (fire-and-forget) -<br/>this reply below never waits<br/>on what happens next
        deactivate Ledger
        activate Projection
        Projection->>Graph: Best-effort write (certificate<br/>node, grant marked consumed) -<br/>a failure here is logged and<br/>ignored, never affects the<br/>reply already on its way - see<br/>graph_projection_catch_up.mmd<br/>for how a missed write is<br/>eventually recovered
        deactivate Projection
        CredAgentCon--)Cassini: Publish issuance event<br/>(fire-and-forget)
    else Already holds a currently valid cert
        Note over CredAgentCon: Refused. A pod cannot request its<br/>own renewal - see "Pods cannot<br/>request their own renewal."
    end

    CredAgentCon--)Cassini: Reply (signed cert, or refusal),<br/>tagged with the original correlation_id,<br/>including the Credentials Agent's<br/>current escrow public key
    deactivate CredAgentCon
    activate Cassini
    Cassini--)CredAgentObs: Deliver correlated reply
    deactivate Cassini
    activate CredAgentObs
    CredAgentObs->>UserTool: Signed certificate (or refusal)
    deactivate CredAgentObs

    activate UserTool
    UserTool->>UserTool: Store cert alongside already-held<br/>private key (e.g. browser NSS import)
    deactivate UserTool

    Note over User,App: Downstream usage (not built today -<br/>shown to confirm the end-to-end vision is coherent)

    User->>App: mTLS request, presenting the<br/>installed certificate
    activate App
    App->>App: Read identity and permission SANs<br/>directly from the cert - zero<br/>further IdP round-trip, zero<br/>dependency on Keycloak, Cassini,<br/>or Neo4j being reachable,<br/>exactly like how Kubernetes<br/>checks a client cert
    App-->>User: Session established
    deactivate App
